econdary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking for and Giving Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are many ways to ask for and to give advice. <br> <br>Here are some expressions you can use to ask for and to give advice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Asking for Advice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Giving Advice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">What do you suggest?</span> <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">How do you suggest I ... ?</span> <br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Do you have any advice for ... ?</span> <br><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What should I bring?</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The best way ...  </span> <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I strongly advise \u2026 </span> <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Why don't you \u2026 </span> <br><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I suggest you bring ... </span>  \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: What should I bring? <br> <span class=\"strong\">Nigel</span>: I suggest you wear a light jacket and hiking boots.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sandra</span>: What should I tell Rob?<br> <span class=\"strong\">Rebecca</span>: You should tell him the cake delivery will be late."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making and Responding to Promises"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When someone makes a promise, they make a commitment to  someone else to doing or not doing something."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Nigel</span>: I promise we'll go ziplining next time we have a school break. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Great! I can't wait!"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You use the Future tense (with will) to make promises.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I'll do the dishes right away.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can also make a promise by using the words \"I promise\" before an action.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I promise to clean my room.</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> I promise I'll do the dishes right away.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can respond to promises with an expression like:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Great!<br/> I believe you.<br/> OK, no problem.<br/> That's fine.<br/> Thanks a lot!</span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cottage "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small vacation home in a rural area"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Thanks for inviting me to this cottage."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about free time activities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to laugh"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to react to a funny situation with sounds and body movement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You make me laugh, Peter."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bungee jumping"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "activity of jumping from a high position holding a strong elastic rope"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I go bungee jumping on weekends."}, {"type": "audio"